Name: partman-cros/no_cros
Type: boolean
Description: Go back to the menu and resume partitioning?
Extended_description: No usable ChromeOS kernel partition is found. At least one such partition is necessary for your machine to be bootable with ChromeOS' verified boot methods (with CTRL+D or CTRL+U). These partitions must reside on the same physical disk as either the root or the boot partition. Two 512 MB partitions should be fine for most installations.\n\nIf you cannot boot into the installed system in another way (like legacy boot with CTRL+L), continuing the installation would result in an unbootable machine.

